text:
The Two SCSS Sections
My custom.scss file has two sections:

/*-- scss:defaults --*/ changes Bootstrap variables, such as the primary color and font.
/*-- scss:rules --*/ adds custom CSS rules for specific classes.

/*-- scss:defaults --*/
$primary: #1b6e5a;

/*-- scss:rules --*/
.skill-badge {
  background: $primary;
  color: white;
  border-radius: 999px;
}

Using a Custom Class in a Page
Quarto’s bracketed spans attach a CSS class to inline text. This is how the skill badges on my home page are styled:
[Team Leadership]{.skill-badge}
